', 'The framework §5.4 named "hybrid" generically. Session 6 must commit to one configuration to evaluate against the 30 criteria — evaluating against the union of configurations would conflate the candidate''s per-criterion scores. H1 was selected over H2 because: (a) H1 aligns with the project''s actual current structure (markdown specifications + structured data); (b) H1''s hybrid-coordination overhead is lowest among hybrid configurations; (c) H1 plausibly tests the eliminator''s pivotal criterion (C-5.2 sentence-level marker enforcement) at score 3 via structured-marker convention, where H2 cannot. The transitivity argument (H2 dismissed if H1 dismissed) is not arbitrary — it follows from the structural fact that operational cost compounds with substrate count and that no criterion in the framework''s §4 inventory uniquely favors RDF-style semantic markup for prose handling.
', '2026-05-02 02:25', 'opus_4_7_session_2026-05-02', 'opus/150/synth', 150, 'ACTIVE', 'PENDING', '[]', '["D-0108"]', '["workplan/b1-candidate-d-hybrid.md \u00a71.3", "sessions/session_2026-05-02-b1-s6.md", "data/decisions/decision_register.yaml"]', '["H2 (RDF + SQLite) \u2014 rejected: doubles up on database-substrate operational burden; does not preserve markdown editing workflow; cannot score 3 on C-5.2 (the elimination pivot) any more than H1 can.", "H3 (Markdown + YAML primary + SQLite read-only mirror auto-generated) \u2014 rejected: this is essentially Candidate A with a derived index, not a hybrid storage form; the storage of record remains markdown+YAML and the SQLite mirror is a query-layer artifact, not architectural.", "Defer the within-D substrate decision to Session 7 (evaluate hybrid abstractly) \u2014 rejected: hybrid abstraction is underspecified for per-criterion evaluation. Sessions 7-9 can revisit only if Candidate D survives elimination."]', 'This decision becomes operationally moot once D-0134 dismisses Candidate D, but is captured for evaluation-trail completeness. The eliminator test outcome depends on which hybrid configuration was tested.
