12 losses against max(A,B,C)). The pivotal criterion C-5.2 showed the hybrid form does not provide structural advantage over Candidate B alone or Candidate A with structured-marker convention; structured-marker convention is form-agnostic.", "Defer the storage-form decision to a later stage (e.g., post-Stage-A close, after A11 counsel review) \u2014 rejected: workplan v3 \u00a7B1 specifies the storage-form decision as the gating commitment for B2-B7 and Stage C. Deferring leaves Stages B and C with no operative form to design tooling against. The PROVISIONAL status of this proposal does the deferring properly: project owner adopts when ready; until adoption, no downstream session commits to the form.", "Apply Rule 1 (highest weighted total wins \u2192 C) \u2014 rejected by D-0137 in Session 7. Mechanical highest-total selection collapses the question into a numeric comparison; ignores doctrinal binding force beyond what weights captured; selects on a 3-point margin (1.7% of max) that is at the noise floor of weighting precision. Rule 3 (tradeoff-aware) was committed by D-0137 specifically to prevent Rule 1''s mechanical resolution of a genuinely contested selection."]', '[RATIFICATION 2026-08-04] ADOPTED by owner directive 2026-08-04 ("ratify all"). This decision has been the operative reality since May: the canonical store is data/guidebook.db, 48 schema migrations have been applied against it, and every generator, check and audit in the repo queries it. Ratification makes the record match the practice rather than changing anything. Its sibling D-0139 (architecture/schema-spec.md) was deliberately NOT ratified in the same act -- see that entry. DG-NON per A12 §2.2 D-DOCT default delegation. Storage form is doctrinal because it governs synthesis structure for 12+ years and reaches into all downstream work (B2 tooling, B3 navigation, B4 pilot, B5 rendering, B6 validation, B7 architecture lock, all of Stage C). The proposal-of-record at architecture/storage-derivation.md is the audit trail for this decision; project-owner adoption converts PROVISIONAL -> CANONICAL.
Adoption may include amendments — the proposed selection may be modified, the rationale refined, or alternatives reconsidered. Amendments are not failures of the proposal; they are how D-DOCT/DG-NON works.
