', 'connection-scout merged into connection-discovery with --mode flag; scout deprecated', 'connection-scout is absorbed into connection-discovery. connection-discovery gains three modes via --mode flag: spec (item specifications and cross-reference tables), evidence (BPC files, gap register, session outputs), external (forward citation search via Scholar Gateway / PubMed). Non-connection findings exit via db.py add-gap, never as SPECULATIVE connections. SPECULATIVE findings are logged as CR gaps per the SPECULATIVE→gap rule. connection-scout_SKILL.md moved to skills/deprecated/.
', 'connection-scout and connection-discovery had overlapping scope (both discover connections from evidence) with the only distinction being internal vs external source material. The --mode flag unifies them under a single skill entry point, reducing the skill registry and eliminating ambiguity about which skill to invoke. Pattern conformance: the merged skill follows the existing db.py CLI output contract.
