', 'The existing functional-deficit-researcher (FDR) skill conducts bottom-up OT intervention research by functional deficit — it synthesizes new evidence into BPC entries. The auditor is a distinct methodological concern: it evaluates whether an item''s existing FDR framing is ICF-aligned and clinically defensible, without conducting new research. This separation follows the project''s general pattern of distinguishing synthesis skills (Opus, generate content) from audit skills (check existing content against criteria). Opus is required because the deficit→spatial requirement judgment chain involves clinical reasoning (e.g., whether hemiplegia→lateral clearance is supported by the cited OT literature), which is beyond checklist application.
', '2026-05-08 03:00', 'opus_4_6_session_2026-05-08', 'opus/100/extract', 100, 'ACTIVE', 'NA', '[]', '["D-0139"]', '["workplan/workplan-item-audit-pipeline-co0009.md \u00a73.2", "workplan/workplan-item-audit-pipeline-co0009.md \u00a72"]', '["Extend functional-deficit-researcher to include audit mode \u2014 rejected: the researcher is a synthesis skill (Opus, generates new BPC content from OT literature). Adding audit responsibilities would conflate generation with evaluation, violating the project''s synthesis/audit separation principle. The researcher produces; the auditor checks.", "Run ICF alignment as a sub-check within evidence-auditor \u2014 rejected: evidence-auditor evaluates evidence quality (stratum, overclaimed markers, uncertain review). ICF alignment is a domain-specific structural check (is the ICF code correct? is the deficit\u2192requirement chain valid?) that requires FDR domain knowledge, not evidence-quality methodology.", "Use Sonnet for the auditor \u2014 rejected: the deficit\u2192requirement judgment is clinical mechanism reasoning. Sonnet handles checklist application (economics-auditor) but ICF alignment requires cross-referencing OT intervention literature against spatial parameters, which is dispersed-evidence synthesis at the judgment level."]', 'Boundary with functional-deficit-researcher: auditor flags items where ICF alignment is questionable; researcher conducts deficit research and synthesizes into BPC. Auditor never generates new BPC content. Skill file to be created in Phase 3.
