', 'Create search_executions logged-search event table plus derived coverage views as the coverage-loop memory; coverage is derived from the log, never hand-written.
', 'Proposed migration 033_search_executions.sql (STRICT + CHECK + json_valid, ships empty, user_version 32->33) mirrored in schemas/search_execution.py, with v_coverage_jurisdiction / v_coverage_language / v_coverage_branch views. Legacy search_coverage / search_languages frozen read-only, not dropped. Migration applied only on owner ratification (PENDING).
', 'Coverage today is two hand-maintained grids (86% NOT-RUN) joined by nothing, with verbatim query text surviving in only ~47 rows; a cell reading SEARCHED cannot prove what was searched. The loop''s success metric (percent required cells with >=1 logged search; percent saturated-or-deferred) is un-fakeable only if coverage is DERIVED from a per-search log. search_executions is that log: deferred_reason makes an honest non-search a counted outcome; admitted_ref_ids gives per-source chain-of-custody and makes spillover routing auditable; explicit executed_at keeps rebuild byte-deterministic. Implements the substrate owner Gate 1 resolved as "thin append-only logger first."
