', 'Research validity is enforced mechanically by research_batch_dod.py (R1-R15), harness hooks and CI, because prose rules degrade as agent context fills.
', 'scripts/audit/research_batch_dod.py implements R1-R15 with a schema-cloning selftest; .claude/settings.json injects the contract at SessionStart and gates at Stop; .github/workflows/research-contract.yml runs the gate plus six previously-unwired enforcers (research_protocol_audit, metadata_integrity_audit, gap_mining_audit, population_integrity_audit, graph_audit, pipeline_contract_audit). All checks non-blocking during shakedown EXCEPT the selftest, which blocks from day one. governance/research-contract-baseline.json discloses inherited debt and ratchets DOWN only.
', 'A nine-batch run skipped Co-1 entirely (co-primary with T1 under CRPD Art 4.3), did zero citation mining, cited zero clauses on quantified regulatory values, and never crossed a population or ICF code — while every one of those rules sat documented in skills/, governance/ and CLAUDE.md. The rules did not fail; prose failed. This confirms finding F1 of the 2026-07-23 enforcement plan (28 enforcers on disk wired to no workflow). Each of R1-R15 restates an existing rule and is traceable to an observed violation, so the mechanism adds enforcement, not doctrine.
', '2026-07-25 04:30', 'owner_directive_2026-07-24_research-validity + opus_session_2026-07-24-research-matrix-completion', 'opus/150/synth', 150, 'ACTIVE', 'PENDING', '[]', '["D-0001", "D-0151"]', '["decisions/DR-2026-07-25-research-contract-mechanical-enforcement.md", "scripts/audit/research_batch_dod.py", ".claude/settings.json", ".github/workflows/research-contract.yml", "governance/research-contract-baseline.json"]', '["Write another methodology document \u2014 rejected; prose is the demonstrated failure mode.", "Make every check blocking immediately \u2014 rejected; violates the spectrum''s shakedown discipline and the false-positive rate is unknown. Only the selftest blocks (no false-positive surface).", "Leave inherited debt failing the gate \u2014 rejected; a permanently-red gate teaches people to ignore it, which is the failure being fixed."]', 'Adversarially attacked before adoption: 8 of 8 attacks succeeded and were fixed (R1 substring false-pass, R2 stub-row gaming, R4 case-insensitive code matching, R8 could never fail, R7/R12 one-row thresholds, R10 ignoring resolution outcome, permanently-red --all, silently-rotted selftest). Design rules recorded in the script. Gate thresholds were authored by the agent whose work they judge — independent review is raised in DR §6.4.
