', 'Adds the 16 compendium fields missing from 037 (design_intent, populations_served_note, outcome_data, conflict_documented, failure_notes, construction_cost, accessible_design_premium, funding_sources, operational_cost_change, remediation_cost, roi_data, financial_evidence_tier, financial_data_quality, evidence_contribution, part13_status, sources) and widens schemas/case_study.py case_study_id to CS-\d{2,4}. No existing identifier renumbered. Applied; user_version 37->38. Table still ships empty.
', 'Migration 037 was built from schemas/case_study.py alone rather than from the prior work. The compendium''s own schema block specifies "id — CS-NN sequential" and holds 26 entries (CS-01..CS-26), so the model''s CS-NNNN pattern — never enforced because no table existed — was the thing out of step, and the validator is widened rather than the corpus renumbered. The larger finding was 16 omitted fields, including the compendium''s entire financial block and its conflict_documented / failure_notes fields: the prior work already had first-class homes for failure evidence and cross-population conflict. The §13.x vs §12 discrepancy was a false conflict (Part 13 in v9.0, Part 12 in v10).
', '2026-07-25 04:45', 'opus_session_2026-07-24-research-matrix-completion', 'opus/125/extract', 125, 'ACTIVE', 'PENDING', '[]', '["D-0155"]', '["scripts/migrations/038_case_study_compendium_reconciliation.sql", "schemas/case_study.py", "references/case-study-compendium.md"]', '["Renumber the 26 compendium entries to CS-NNNN \u2014 rejected; breaks every \u00a713.x cross-reference to satisfy a validator that had no table behind it.", "Leave 037 as-is and map fields at ingest time \u2014 rejected; the omitted financial block is half the compendium''s purpose and would have been silently dropped."]', 'Closes DR-2026-07-25 §6.1. Ingesting the 26 existing compendium entries is follow-on work, not done here; the table remains empty so nothing is asserted.
', '2026-08-04 19:55', 'session_2026-08-04-f3a-decision-register-import', '2026-08-04 19:55', 'session_2026-08-04-f3a-decision-register-import');
', 'ADOPTED by owner directive 2026-08-04 ("ratify all"). Vocabulary and definitions are settled; the implementing migration has NOT run, so B01/B02/B05 stay red until it does. Adopts a BINARY verification_status in {VERIFIED, UNVERIFIED}, a new verification_disposition in {OPEN, CLOSED}, and the existing verification_attempt_count as the third column of that set, plus a verification_method column recording how a standing was established. Retires VERIFIED-1, VERIFIED-2, VERIFIED-WITH-CORRECTION, UNVERIFIED-1, UNVERIFIED-CLOSED, SUPERSEDED, DISPUTED and PARTIAL — every intermediate value turns out to be another column in disguise. Defines VERIFIED for the first time as "the document itself was obtained and the metadata recorded here was read from it". Ratifies source_type ''code''. B01/B02/B05 in test_db_integrity stay red until ratified.
', 'Asked to ratify the session-coined vocabulary, the owner rejected the premise: grades of VERIFIED mean either the sources are not properly verified or the definition of verified is broken. Both were true. The column encodes three orthogonal facts at once — what is established, how, and how hard anyone tried — the same conflation migration 041 fixed for author_display/publisher/standard_number ("a column must hold one domain"). Evidence is decisive: UNVERIFIED-1 claims one search attempt while 25 of its 31 rows have verification_attempt_count = 0, and its documented meaning (evidence-methodology.md section 204, "one search attempt, not yet retried") is not what the owner inferred reading it cold — an encoding ambiguous and wrong at once. VERIFIED-1 differs from canonical UNVERIFIED-1 by two characters while meaning the opposite. VERIFIED-WITH-CORRECTION describes an event already recorded in verification_note. VERIFIED-2''s 71 rows are honestly documented but the document was never obtained, so they are not verified. Separating the columns makes the tuple self-auditing and immediately surfaces that 360 of 824 VERIFIED-family rows (43%) record zero attempts — 135 of them a tool-counter defect that can simply be backfilled.
', '2026-08-04 00:45', 'owner_jordanelias_directive_2026-08-04', 'opus/200/arbitrate', 200, 'ACTIVE', 'NA', '[]', '["D-0156"]', '["decisions/DR-2026-08-04-verification-status-is-a-standing-not-a-history.md"]', '["Ratify the coined values and amend the check \u2014 rejected by the owner; entrenches the conflation without a decision record.\n", "Rewrite the 71 VERIFIED-2 rows to plain VERIFIED \u2014 destroys a distinction recorded deliberately and overstates the corpus.\n", "A boolean blocked_permanent flag instead of a disposition column \u2014 superseded by the owner''s OPEN/CLOSED formulation, which pairs with status and makes closure auditable against attempt count.\n", "Leave B01/B02/B05 red indefinitely \u2014 the status quo, and the fallback if not ratified.\n"]', 'DG-NON because it defines what counts as verified evidence. Consequence the owner should weigh explicitly: the corpus "verified" count falls by at least 71 (~8%) and possibly further. Nothing is lost — same sources, same notes, same real work — the headline number falls because it was overstated. Zero published cells cite a VERIFIED-2 source, so no cell state and no rendered page changes. DISPUTED is left unchanged as an open question.
', '2026-08-04 19:55', 'session_2026-08-04-f3a-decision-register-import', '2026-08-04 19:55', 'session_2026-08-04-f3a-decision-register-import');
', 'ADOPTED by owner directive 2026-08-12 ("product cell as (item x population) is confusing terminology. rename to specification"). Executed: schema version 055 as a version marker, its DDL in the paired data migration data_20260812075349_2026-08-12-rename-cell-to-specification.sql, and schema version 056 carrying an AFTER_DATA marker that reopens the numbered schema phase on the post-rename names. Both tables held 0 rows, so no row moved. From 057 onward, ordinary numbered schema migrations may name `specifications` and `specification_source_links` normally.
', '"Cell" was the matrix framing and collided with the vocabulary already in use everywhere else (spec_page.py, spec_value_probes, case_study_specs, economics_entry_specs, specs/) and with the Specification layer that armature_v4_resolutions.md reserves by name. The replay half was forced, not chosen: migrate_db.py applied all schema migrations before any data migration, and 19 committed immutable data migrations still write the old names, so a schema-phase rename broke `--rebuild` with `no such table: evidence_cell_state`. Migration 025 records the same collision from the other side.
', '2026-08-12 08:40', 'owner_jordanelias_directive_2026-08-12', 'opus/200/arbitrate', 200, 'ACTIVE', 'NA', '[]', '["D-0157"]', '["decisions/DR-2026-08-12-specification-rename-and-replay-order.md", "workplan/2026-08-12-step-R-rename-execution-record.md"]', '["Rename in the schema phase and accept a broken rebuild \u2014 refused; a permanently red blocking gate is a disarmed gate.\n", "Withdraw or rewrite the 19 old-name data migrations \u2014 refused; they are append-only and immutable once committed.\n", "Leave the DDL in the data phase with the invariant only documented \u2014 refused; it walls the two central tables off from the numbered schema phase forever and turns every future constraint into a data migration.\n", "A compatibility view named evidence_cell_state with INSTEAD OF triggers, dropped at the end of replay \u2014 refused; its fidelity is unverifiable in the direction that matters and it returns a dead name to sqlite_master.\n", "A schema + data baseline squashing the history \u2014 deferred, not refused: it is the larger clean answer, it needs a runner change for data-migration supersession that does not exist today, and it is a separate owner decision. AFTER_DATA does not foreclose it.\n"]', 'Enforcement is mechanical, not remembered: evidence_cell_state and cell_source_links are RV-020/RV-021 in governance/retired-vocabulary.yaml at severity `broken`, so the residual sweep is a standing check. cell_id is recorded in that file''s `rejected:` section - it fails admission test 4 because architecture/schema-spec.md''s aspirational `cell` table declares its own cell_id and no regex separates the two.
', '2026-08-12 08:40', 'session_2026-08-12-specification-rename', '2026-08-12 08:40', 'session_2026-08-12-specification-rename');
